{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`model_max_output_tokens` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`, `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`) knows only the three Claude ladder models and falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS` (16,000) for an unmapped model. Amazon Nova models on Bedrock accept at most 10,000 output tokens, so every review call that rides the \"raise to model max\" seam with a Nova model is rejected by Bedrock with `ValidationException: The maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 10000` before it runs — measured live during the 2026-08-11 model-comparison experiments (rebar ticket b902-18af-14ed-4da1), where the whole plan-review LLM phase collapsed to INDETERMINATE until the table was patched in-process. Nova Pro subsequently completed 8/8 end-to-end plan-review replays, so the ceiling entry is the only blocker to running these models through rebar.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd three entries to `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`: `(\"nova-pro\", 10_000)`, `(\"nova-lite\", 10_000)`, `(\"nova-micro\", 10_000)` (substring match covers the Bedrock inference-profile ids like `us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0`, and `nova-lite` covers `nova-2-lite`). Values per the AWS Bedrock model documentation: Nova family max output tokens = 10,000. No behavior change for any currently-configured model: the table is consulted only when the resolved model matches an entry, and the existing conservative fallback stays for everything else.\n\nExtend the existing unit coverage of `model_max_output_tokens` with the Nova ids (full Bedrock profile-id form and bare form).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `model_max_output_tokens(\"bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0\")` returns 10000. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'src'); from rebar.llm.review_kernel.verify import model_max_output_tokens as f; assert f('bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0')==10000 and f('us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0')==10000 and f('claude-sonnet-4-6')==128000\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] A unit test pins the Nova entries alongside the existing Claude entries. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py -x` passes.\n- [ ] Unknown models still fall back to the configured default (existing behavior pinned by an assertion in the same test). Verify: same pytest run passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786471364184976001,"uuid":"82145e3d-c686-462b-aab1-6af3f1217b3d"}